{"actor":"orchestrator","data":{"gate":"design_approval","gate_key":"design_approval:5","summary":"Add GET /api/v1/links as a new handler on the existing LinkController. It returns a bare JSON array of up to `limit` links (default 20, range 1..100), newest first. Items are the same LinkResponse DTO, built by the same mapping as GET /api/v1/links/{code}. Data access is one bounded JPQL query on LinkRepository. The query orders by createdAt DESC, id DESC, applies the same retrievability predicate that LinkService uses for the {code} lookup, and is capped with Spring Data `Limit` so filtering happens before limiting. A thin LinkService method supplies the same 'now' time source used by the existing gone/expiry check. The controller reads `limit` as a raw String so that an absent parameter can be told apart from an empty one. Invalid values (empty, non-integer, out of range) are rejected before any data access by throwing ResponseStatusException(400), which renders as an RFC 9457 ProblemDetail through the existing GlobalExceptionHandler. The codebase has no security configuration (no SecurityConfig class exists), so access-control parity with GET /{code} holds without changes. There are no schema changes and no new dependencies."},"dedupe_key":"design_approval:5:req","event":"approval_requested","hash":"a8d37fd2913733d1f6ae5422f127ae1e7a2db3ea4aaa196b7715328b0e662882","parent_span_id":null,"prev_hash":"f3c238561511ac7feea3f8a3557b252601039452d6530059a20891a9026e4a65","run_id":"live-recent-links","seq":26,"span_id":"c775d54419614af7","stage":"design_approval","trace_id":"live-recent-links","ts":"2026-10-30T16:54:48.906+00:00"}
