{"actor":"orchestrator","data":{"gate":"design_approval","gate_key":"design_approval:7","summary":"Add GET /api/v1/links to the existing LinkController. It returns a bare JSON array of LinkResponse items, newest first, bounded by limit (default 20, range 1..100).\n\nThe list applies no visibility predicate. GET /api/v1/links/{code} goes through LinkService.get(), which throws only LinkNotFoundException and also returns expired and deactivated links. So every persisted link is retrievable by code, and the list returns all links ordered by createdAt DESC, id DESC.\n\nThe repository bounds the query at the database level with a derived Spring Data query that takes a Limit.\n\nlimit is bound as a request parameter. Range violations throw InvalidUrlException, following the AnalyticsService 'days' convention; it is already mapped to a 400 ProblemDetail. Non-integer values are already rejected with 400 through MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException. An empty 'limit=' is detected explicitly and rejected the same way.\n\nNo changes are made to GlobalExceptionHandler, LinkResponse, the schema, or security; there is no security configuration in the codebase. Tests are a single MockMvc integration class under @ActiveProfiles(\"test\"). It uses TestClockConfig/MutableClock to control createdAt."},"dedupe_key":"design_approval:7:req","event":"approval_requested","hash":"287c4d5bcf6e090368d0eb4483d812b5aa3b0ba163af78af56e91d1354d0633d","parent_span_id":null,"prev_hash":"d305fcf0abad65fc68fc78753248487249d109ab42adf2366b8d3bac3b591945","run_id":"live-recent-links","seq":36,"span_id":"d77fab09144940c8","stage":"design_approval","trace_id":"live-recent-links","ts":"2026-10-30T16:56:28.884+00:00"}
