{"actor":"orchestrator","data":{"gate":"release_approval","gate_key":"release_approval:13","summary":"Adds GET /api/v1/links, which returns a bare JSON array of LinkResponse items ordered newest first, with a limit parameter that defaults to 20 and accepts 1..100.\n\nT1: LinkRepository gets a derived query, findAllByOrderByCreatedAtDescIdDesc(Limit). The database applies ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC and LIMIT n, and no count query runs. No visibility predicate is applied, because LinkService.get() (behind GET /{code}) returns every persisted link, including inactive and expired ones.\n\nT2:\n- LinkService.listRecent(int) checks 1..100 before any repository access. A violation throws the existing InvalidUrlException, which is already mapped to a 400 application/problem+json response.\n- The new LinkController handler uses 20 only when the parameter is absent. An empty 'limit=' is rejected with InvalidUrlException. Non-integer values fail Integer binding and go through the existing type-mismatch 400 handling.\n- Items are built with LinkResponse.from(link, properties.baseUrl()), the same call GET /{code} makes.\n\nT3: The codebase has no security configuration, so no config file changes. The T3 change is a test showing the list endpoint gets the same unauthenticated 200 as GET /{code}.\n\nT4: Tests for the repository query cover ordering by createdAt rather than insertion order, a deterministic tie-break, the bounded row count, the empty result, and inactive and expired links being included.\n\nT5: A MockMvc integration class covers:\n- array shape and ordering, including non-increasing createdAt\n- the empty [] result\n- default, explicit, 1 and 100 limits\n- rejection of 0, 101, -1, abc, 1.5 and an empty value, each with no link data and no side effects\n- JSON equality with GET /{code}\n- visibility parity: 30 links, the 10 newest deactivated or expired, limit=20\n- identical results for two callers\n\nNo changes to GlobalExceptionHandler, LinkResponse, the sc